<title>USA: Alliant Techsystems wins $17.3 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Alliant Techsystems wins $17.3 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alliant Techsystems Inc said Tuesday its Conventional Munitions Group has been awarded a $17.3 million contract from Hughes Missile Systems Co to produce rocket motors and heavy warheads for the AGM 65 Maverick Air-to-Ground Missile.</p>
<p>Hughes Missile Systems is a unit of Hughes Electronics Corp, which is a subsidiary of General Motors Corp.</p>
<p>Additional sales of the missile to the U.S. government and to allied nations could increase the total value of the contract to more than $25 million over the next five years according to estimates by Hughes Missile, Alliant said.</p>
<p>Deliveries are expected to begin in April 1998.</p>
<p>		   ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
